// A let-extract flip (soak nov25a): with the fold's callback named and passed
// by name, the select was refused "{ c: '_, n: List<'_> } could go to more
// than one member of the union". Calling a named function that reads `v0.c`
// joins `c`'s cell to the function's own variable, and a cell that reached a
// scheme's variable waited for it even at the input's end, where every scheme
// has closed: the value among the patterns was never placed. At an input's
// end a scheme's variable holds nothing back.
// Expected trace (both engines): 43.
{ let v0 = { c: cast<i64>(z64:1 + z64:42)$, n: [<-1.0 * 2.0>] }; let v1: f64 = select v0 { { c: 2, n: [<_>] } => 1.0, { c: _, n: v3 } => 2.5 }; let tm = |v2, v3| v0.c; array::fold([-1, 42, 2], 7, tm) }
